M_README_MD = '# textreel\n\nA small rule-based text annotation engine. Given a piece of text it\ntokenizes the input, runs a stack of named rules over the tokens, merges the\nresulting matches into non-overlapping annotations, and reports those\nannotations together with the evidence that produced them.\n\ntextreel is a library, not a service. The engine is deterministic for a\ngiven configuration and input: same text, same rules, same annotations, in\nthe same order.\n\n## Quick start\n\n```ts\nimport { TextReel } from "textreel";\n\nconst reel = new TextReel({\n  rules: [\n    { id: "phone-us", pattern: "phone", country: "US", action: "mask" }\n  ]\n});\n\nconst result = reel.run("Call 555-010-9999 during office hours.");\nfor (const ann of result.annotations()) {\n  console.log(ann.category, ann.span.start, ann.span.end, ann.label);\n}\n```\n\n## Repository layout\n\n```\nsrc/\n  core/       span, token and index primitives\n  rules/      pattern compilation, matching, rule chains\n  engine/     the TextReel entry point, sessions, cache, reports\n  ops/        normalization, tokenization, classification, scoring, merging\n  config/     configuration parsing, defaults, validation, presets\n  cli/        a small command line front end\n  index.ts    public surface\ntests/        vitest suite (one file per module)\ndocs/         design notes and API reference\n```\n\n## Public API (top level)\n\nThe public surface lives in `src/index.ts` and is documented in\n`docs/api.md`. The short contract:\n\n| Member | Signature |\n|---|---|\n| `TextReel(config)` | constructor; accepts a `ReelConfig` object |\n| `reel.config()` | resolved configuration; never `undefined` once constructed |\n| `reel.run(text)` | tokenizes, matches and merges; returns a `ReelResult` |\n| `reel.resolve(id)` | `Annotation | undefined`; an id that was never emitted resolves to `undefined` |\n| `reel.stats()` | live counters (`ReelStats`) |\n| `result.annotations()` | ordered list of `Annotation` objects |\n| `result.tokens()` | tokens the run produced |\n| `result.top(n)` | the `n` highest-scoring annotations |\n\n## Configuration\n\n`ReelConfig` has three optional keys (defaults apply when omitted):\n\n- `rules` — rule descriptors (each descriptor is partial; missing fields fall\n  back to rule defaults).\n- `categoryWeights` — multipliers per category applied when scoring matches.\n- `options` — engine switches (`caseSensitive`, `maxMatches`, `cacheSize`).\n\n`resolvedConfig()`/`config()` never return `undefined`; the loader merges the\nuser object over a complete default configuration.\n\n## Development\n\nInstall dependencies once (there is no network at trial time):\n\n```sh\nnpm install\nnpm test        # type-checks, then runs the vitest suite\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- The tokenizer supports the built-in kinds listed in `src/ops/kinds.ts`.\n- Rule matching is case-insensitive unless `options.caseSensitive` is set.\n- The default `cacheSize` is 64 and the cache is bounded.\n'


M_DOCS_API_MD = '# API reference\n\nText above, code below. Only `src/index.ts` names and the value objects they\nreturn are part of the supported surface.\n\n## TextReel\n\n```ts\nnew TextReel(config?: ReelConfig)\n```\n\n- `config()` : `ResolvedConfig` — never `undefined`.\n- `run(text: string, cursor?: RunOptions)` : `ReelResult`\n- `resolve(id: string)` : `Annotation | undefined`\n- `stats()` : `ReelStats`\n- `rules()` : `Rule[]` — normalized rules in priority order.\n- `pattern(id: string)` : `Pattern | undefined`\n\n## ReelResult\n\n- `annotations()` : `Annotation[]`\n- `tokens()` : `Token[]`\n- `top(n: number)` : `Annotation[]`\n- `matchedText(annotation: Annotation)` : `string`\n- `text()` : `string`\n- `summary()` : `string` — one line per annotation.\n\n## Value objects\n\n- `Span { start: number; end: number }` — half-open offsets.\n- `Annotation { id: string; category: string; label: string;\n  span: Span; score: number; evidence: string[] }`\n- `Match { ruleId: string; patternId: string; span: Span;\n  groups: Record<string, string>; score: number; label: string }`\n- `Pattern { id: string; source: string; kind: string; flags: string;\n  priority: number; group?: string }`\n- `Rule { id: string; category: string; action: string; weight: number;\n  enabled: boolean; patterns: Pattern[]; note?: string }`\n- `ReelStats { runs: number; cacheHits: number; cacheMisses: number;\n  matches: number; tornDown: number }`\n- `ResolvedConfig { rules: Rule[]; categoryWeights: Record<string, number>;\n  options: ReelOptions; builtAt: string }`\n- `ReelOptions { caseSensitive: boolean; maxMatches: number;\n  cacheSize: number; mergeStrategy: string; keepEvidence: boolean }`\n'


M_DOCS_ARCHITECTURE_MD = '# Design notes\n\n## Pipeline\n\nA single `run` goes through five stages:\n\n1. **normalize** — optional case folding and whitespace collapsing.\n2. **tokenize** — one forward scan; the scanner takes the longest match at\n   each position, consulting the kind registry (see `src/ops/kinds.ts`).\n3. **match** — every rule is tried over the tokens. A rule whose patterns\n   all match at the same span contributes one `Match` with its captures.\n4. **merge** — overlapping matches from lower-priority rules are dropped\n   unless the higher-priority annotation accepts multi-labels.\n5. **annotate** — surviving matches become `Annotation` records with an\n   evidence list and a score.\n\n## Scoring\n\n`scoreMatch` combines three signals:\n\n- frequency: how often the matched text occurs in the input;\n- length: longer matches score slightly higher (ties broken by earlier\n  start, then by rule priority);\n- category weight: the per-category multiplier from the resolved config.\n\nScores are clamped to `[0, 100]` and rounded to three decimals.\n\n## Span model\n\nSpans are half-open `[start, end)` character offsets. The `SortedIndex`\nkeeps tokens sorted by `(start, end)` and answers range queries in\n`O(log n + k)`. Overlapping annotations are resolved in `merge.ts` by\nwalking the index neighbours of each candidate.\n\n## Caching\n\nThe engine keeps a bounded result cache keyed by the SHA-1 of the input\ntext. On a warm cache the tokenize/match stages are skipped entirely; the\nreported result object is still produced fresh so callers never mutate\nshared state.\n\n## Failure mode\n\nAll engine failures are reported with `LedaError` values with a stable\n`code`. Config problems surface like a list of `LoadError` records from\n`validateConfig`; the loader never throws for user data.\n'


